  "name": " Vitamin D3",
  "code": " Vitamin D3",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<ul><li style=\"font-size: 10px;\">If the serum vitamin D3 level is within the normal range, it typically indicates that the body's vitamin D levels are balanced, and the risk of developing bone-related disorders such as osteoporosis is lower.</li><li style=\"font-size: 10px;\">If the serum vitamin D3 level is below the normal range, it may indicate vitamin D deficiency, which can be caused by factors such as inadequate dietary intake, lack of sunlight exposure, malabsorption, or certain medical conditions. Vitamin D deficiency can increase the risk of developing bone-related disorders and other health problems.</li><li style=\"font-size: 10px;\">If the serum vitamin D3 level is above the normal range, it may indicate vitamin D toxicity, which can cause a variety of symptoms such as nausea, vomiting, weakness, and kidney damage. Vitamin D toxicity is rare and usually occurs only with excessive supplementation.</li></ul>",
